('stat-bass-summary','dataset_summary','PSI-26','BASS test outcomes summary (derived)','BASS flight tests: 130. Tests whose observations mention ignition: 71; flame spread: 20; extinguishment: 43 (keyword-derived, approximate). O2 range 15.9-22.7% at about 0.98 atm. Most common materials: 2 cm sphere (18), PMMA sphere 2 cm (10), SIBAL 2 cm (9), Japan Wax Candle, wake (8), PMMA 2 cm (8), 1 cm sphere (6).','https://psi.nasa.gov/physci/repo/data/investigations/PSI-26',''),
('stat-saffire3-summary','dataset_summary','PSI-100','Saffire-III telemetry summary (derived)','Saffire-III telemetry: 11450 rows at 1 sample/s, 1405 active (non-baseline) rows, 1010 rows with smoke_flag, 17 rows with igniter_on. Channels: 4 radiometers, 2 airflow, fan, temperature, smoke obscuration/scatter, 9 igniter currents. Flags are threshold-derived, not NASA labels.','','');
